From: Farhan Ali <alifm@linux.ibm.com>
Subject: KVM: s390: pci: Fix missing error codes and memory unaccounting
Patch-mainline: v7.2-rc6
Git-commit: f86842e4d6c482300f4567f492d512c9ccf5bc4f
References: bsc#1277451

Description: KVM/s390/pci: Fix resource leaks and cleanup in error paths
Symptom: resource leaks, denial-of-service
Problem: Error paths in interrupt forwarding logic for passthrough PCI devices
         failed to cleanup resources correctly.       
Solution: Fix the logic and handle cleanup appropriately.      
Reproduction:  -

Upstream-Description:

              KVM: s390: pci: Fix missing error codes and memory unaccounting

              In kvm_s390_pci_aif_enable() two error paths failed to set an error code,
              causing the function to return 0 on failure. It also failed to rollback
              memory accounting on failure. Fix both by propagating an error code on
              failure and calling unaccount_mem() in the cleanup path.

              Fixes: 3c5a1b6f0a18 ("KVM: s390: pci: provide routines for enabling/disabling interrupt forwarding")
              Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
              Reviewed-by: Christian Borntraeger <borntraeger@linux.ibm.com>
              Reviewed-by: Matthew Rosato <mjrosato@linux.ibm.com>
              Signed-off-by: Farhan Ali <alifm@linux.ibm.com>
              Tested-by: Matthew Rosato <mjrosato@linux.ibm.com>
              Signed-off-by: Christian Borntraeger <borntraeger@linux.ibm.com>


Signed-off-by: Farhan Ali <alifm@linux.ibm.com>
Acked-by: Hannes Reinecke <hare@suse.de>
---
 arch/s390/kvm/pci.c |    9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/s390/kvm/pci.c
+++ b/arch/s390/kvm/pci.c
@@ -302,14 +302,17 @@ static int kvm_s390_pci_aif_enable(struc
 	}
 
 	/* Account for pinned pages, roll back on failure */
-	if (account_mem(zdev->kzdev, pcount))
+	rc = account_mem(zdev->kzdev, pcount);
+	if (rc)
 		goto unpin2;
 
 	/* AISB must be allocated before we can fill in GAITE */
 	mutex_lock(&aift->aift_lock);
 	bit = airq_iv_alloc_bit(aift->sbv);
-	if (bit == -1UL)
+	if (bit == -1UL) {
+		rc = -ENOMEM;
 		goto unlock;
+	}
 	zdev->aisb = bit; /* store the summary bit number */
 	zdev->aibv = airq_iv_create(msi_vecs, AIRQ_IV_DATA |
 				    AIRQ_IV_BITLOCK |
@@ -353,6 +356,8 @@ static int kvm_s390_pci_aif_enable(struc
 	return rc;
 
 unlock:
+	if (pcount > 0)
+		unaccount_mem(zdev->kzdev, pcount);
 	mutex_unlock(&aift->aift_lock);
 unpin2:
 	if (fib->fmt0.sum == 1)
